# Paths excluded from scripts/deploy_to_jetson.sh, on top of .gitignore.
#
# Syntax follows .gitignore/.dockerignore:
#   pattern      exclude it
#   /pattern     anchor to the repo root
#   pattern/     directories only
#   !pattern     re-include something an earlier rule (or .gitignore) excluded
#   # comment    ignored
#
# Two rsync notes:
#   - Excluding a path here does not delete an already-deployed copy on the
#     Jetson. Remove it there by hand once.
#   - To re-include a file inside an excluded directory, re-include the
#     directory first: "!config/", then "!config/keep.toml".

# Examples:
/docs/
/logo/
/stickers/
/.claude/
/.serena/
/build/
/build-test/
/build-docker/
# The e-CAM25 camera driver is vendored source that the Jetson builds itself, so
# it has to ship. rsync reads .gitignore but not its "!" negation, so the
# re-include lives here, and it has to come before the exclusion below because
# the first matching rule wins.
!/third_party/
!/third_party/ecam25/
!/third_party/ecam25/**
# Foxglove SDK is architecture-specific; the Jetson installs its own via
# scripts/install_jetson.sh.
/third_party/
